{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:102218","published":"2026-11-23T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-23T14:00:02.872937353Z","related":["CVE-2026-64487","CVE-2026-72084","CVE-2026-74394","CVE-2026-90294","CVE-2026-90413","CVE-2026-90414","CVE-2026-92508","CVE-2026-92511","CVE-2026-93054","CVE-2026-98549","CVE-2026-99235","CVE-2026-99288","CVE-2026-99661"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-64487","CVE-2026-72084","CVE-2026-74394","CVE-2026-90294","CVE-2026-90413","CVE-2026-90414","CVE-2026-92508","CVE-2026-92511","CVE-2026-93054","CVE-2026-98549","CVE-2026-99235","CVE-2026-99288","CVE-2026-99661"],"summary":"Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: ALSA: caiaq: fix out-of-bounds read in the Traktor Kontrol S4 input parser (CVE-2026-64487)\n  * kernel: scsi: target: Bound PR-OUT TransportID parsing to the received buffer (CVE-2026-72084)\n  * kernel: RDMA/srpt: fix integer overflow in immediate data length check (CVE-2026-74394)\n  * kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq() (CVE-2026-92508)\n  * kernel: uio: Fix stale info pointer in failed registration path (CVE-2026-93054)\n  * kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_destroy_cq_user() (CVE-2026-92511)\n  * kernel: IB/isert: reject login PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90413)\n  * kernel: IB/isert: reject PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90414)\n  * kernel: IB/isert: delay the final Login Response until the session is registered (CVE-2026-90294)\n  * kernel: tcp: prevent collapsing skbs across boundary in rtx queue (CVE-2026-98549)\n  * kernel: kernel: Privilege escalation via use-after-free in event tracing subsystem (CVE-2026-99235)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via race condition in TCP socket lookup (CVE-2026-99288)\n  * kernel: kernel: Memory corruption via integer overflow in GUP-fast (CVE-2026-99661)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [RHEL-8.10.z] RDMA/ulps: Backport security fixes (JIRA:RHEL-289994)\n  * [RHEL-8.10.z] RDMA: Backport security fixes (JIRA:RHEL-296076)\n  * [AlmaLinux 8.10] Incorrect swap size value in /proc/swaps if swap area is very big (JIRA:RHEL-302561)\n  * lockd: fix vfs_test_lock() calls (JIRA:RHEL-304667)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bpftool","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/bpftool"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.189.1.el8_10"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:102218.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.189.1.el8_10"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:102218.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-abi-stablelists","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-abi-stablelists"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.189.1.el8_10"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:102218.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-core","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-core"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.189.1.el8_10"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:102218.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-cross-headers","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-c